## What I found (top level)

**The product doesn't exist at the UI layer.** For an app whose premise is "least-processed sensor data, developed by our own code", there is **no ISO, no shutter speed, no white balance, no manual focus, no histogram, no clipping meter, no focus reticle, no AE/AF lock, no level, no lens selection**. The only exposure control is a ±3 EV bias on Apple's auto-exposure (`CameraView.swift:41-52`). Halide, Kino, Obscura, Leica LUX and Adobe Indigo all ship ISO + shutter + WB.

**Three P0 accessibility failures, computed not eyeballed:**
- HUD captions have **no backing** — white @85% directly on the preview (`CameraHUDButton.swift:22-24`) = **1.1:1** on a white sky. The shutter is pure white = **1.0:1**.
- Zoom/aspect chips white on `black.opacity(0.5)` = **3.98:1** (fails AA 4.5:1). EV bubble yellow on `black.opacity(0.55)` = **4.43:1**.
- Grep-verified zeros: `relativeTo`/Dynamic Type (9 hard-coded fonts), haptics, Reduce Motion/Contrast/Transparency, `minWidth`/`minHeight`, `safeAreaInset`, `accessibilityAdjustableAction`. `GalleryView.swift` has **zero** `accessibilityLabel`.

**The layout lies.** The 16:9 aperture mask is computed over the full screen (`.ignoresSafeArea()`) while the chrome covers the lower ~190pt of that same rect — ~26% of the "chosen" frame is behind the controls, and develop-time `PrintCrop` crops exactly that.

**The "design system" is 212 lines of enum + string registry**, referencing five token files that don't exist; `ControlIDRegistry` is used by no view. The lint that polices it **reports 777 violations across 51 lines, and 6 of its own 26 tests fail** — including a provably broken 44pt checker that can only ever emit `0.0pt`, and a symbol parser that emits `Image(systemName: "camera.aperture)")`.

**Also:** zoom chips promise 2× detail the capture doesn't contain (1× + crop); the shutter silently cancels the self-timer; the volume-button shutter is dead at volume 0 and 1; landscape is enabled in `project.yml:53` and completely unhandled; the UI test target is missing from the checked-in scheme so 812 lines of UI tests have silently stopped running.

The doc ends with a concrete target spec: 7 screens, camera layout zones with pt values, a control-state table, a gesture↔button equivalence matrix, a minimal 6-part token set justified from first principles, and a benchmark table citing Halide's actual support docs.
